🔥 Difference Between Array and ArrayList in Java
🔹 1️⃣ Array
✅ Key Points:

Fixed size (cannot grow/shrink after creation)

Can store primitive and object types

Faster than ArrayList

Part of core Java (not Collection framework)

Example:
int[] arr = new int[3];
arr[0] = 10;
arr[1] = 20;
arr[2] = 30;

👉 Size is fixed (3). Cannot add more elements.

🔹 2️⃣ ArrayList

Class from Java Collection Framework

Located in java.util package

Dynamic size (can grow automatically)

Can store objects only (not primitives directly)

Example:
import java.util.ArrayList;

ArrayList<Integer> list = new ArrayList<>();
list.add(10);
list.add(20);
list.add(30);

👉 Size increases automatically.
